     6	def smallest_change(arr):
     7	    """
     8	    Given an array arr of integers, find the minimum number of elements that
     9	    need to be changed to make the array palindromic. A palindromic array is an array that
    10	    is read the same backwards and forwards. In one change, you can change one element to any other element.
    11	
    12	    For example:
    13	    smallest_change([1,2,3,5,4,7,9,6]) == 4
    14	    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 4, 3, 2, 2]) == 1
    15	    smallest_change([1, 2, 3, 2, 1]) == 0
    16	    """
